  "description": "Shenora: the hybrid app framework for .NET + React, portable across Windows, Android and iOS — reference it plus ONE shell package. Three layers: Core is the contract (the typed IPC stack with its middleware dispatcher and scoped router, the event bus, the webview interception and file-serving pipeline, and the platform-neutral shell contracts — the IUiDispatcher UI-thread seam plus file dialogs, clipboard, URL launching and UI blocking, so application logic compiles with no Windows reference). Engine is the brain (the mission scheduler with claims, lanes and durable queues; journalled safe file mutation with path locks). Modules bridge .NET to the web (media probing, planning, remuxing, streamed range delivery and platform codec conversion; native file dialogs; Live Activities and playback sessions; request tracking; staged self-update with safe archive extraction; versioned resource packs whose boot decision cannot skip the packaged-vs-fetched version comparison). Application host and builder via ShenoraApplication.CreateBuilder. Depends on Microsoft.Extensions DI (implementation) + logging abstractions.",
